{
 "dur": 73.4,
 "vo": [
  {
   "id": "v01",
   "t": 0.4,
   "chunks": [
    "How does a jet engine push",
    "an airliner through the sky?",
    "Let's take one apart."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v02",
   "t": 5.38,
   "chunks": [
    "This is a turbofan,",
    "the engine on almost every airliner.",
    "Its job: grab a huge amount of air,",
    "and throw it out the back, fast."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v03",
   "t": 13.86,
   "chunks": [
    "Up front, the giant fan.",
    "Most of the air it pulls in",
    "never enters the core.",
    "It flows around it.",
    "That's bypass air,",
    "and it makes most of the thrust."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v04",
   "t": 23.48,
   "chunks": [
    "The rest enters the core.",
    "Rows of compressor blades squeeze it,",
    "stage after stage,",
    "to over 30 times outside pressure."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v05",
   "t": 31.71,
   "chunks": [
    "In the combustor,",
    "fuel sprays into that squeezed air",
    "and burns nonstop,",
    "like a blowtorch that never goes out."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v06",
   "t": 38.98,
   "chunks": [
    "The hot gas blasts through the turbine",
    "and spins it.",
    "Shafts carry that power forward",
    "to drive the compressor and fan."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v07",
   "t": 46.31,
   "chunks": [
    "Then it rushes out the nozzle.",
    "Air goes back,",
    "so the engine goes forward.",
    "Newton's third law."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v08",
   "t": 52.51,
   "chunks": [
    "Suck, squeeze, bang, blow.",
    "All at once, all the time."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v09",
   "t": 56.38,
   "chunks": [
    "The Boeing 737's CFM56:",
    "a five-foot fan,",
    "about five times more air around the core",
    "than through it,",
    "and up to 27,000 pounds of thrust."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v10",
   "t": 68.56,
   "chunks": [
    "Congrats! You've discovered",
    "the jet engine."
   ]
  }
 ]
}